<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan firm starting ferry to Spain.</title>
<headline>Moroccan firm starting ferry to Spain.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's privately-owned shipping company Limadet Ferry will start a passenger and car ferry service between the northern town of Nador and Almeria in Spain on April 15, the Tangier-based company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said its 1,300 passenger-ship Beni Ansar would do the trip three times each day in the summer, and twice daily in non-peak periods. The ship can carry 350 cars, it added.</p>
</text>
